Checking review report replies for PR #42...

============================================================
  Review Report Requires a Reply
============================================================

The newest automated review report has not been addressed:

  - comment 100 by @github-actions[bot], posted 2026-08-05T10:00:00Z
    https://github.com/rediacc/console/pull/42#issuecomment-100

------------------------------------------------------------
WHY THIS BLOCKS. This is the pipeline's report for the head it
reviewed. It is a top-level comment, so it has no thread and
nothing to resolve: the only evidence anyone read it is a
later comment answering it. There is none.

READ THE REVIEWER'S OWN SUMMARY TOO. The same pass usually
posts a SEPARATE summary comment carrying the findings, and
this report can be just a wrap-up. List both before replying:

  gh api repos/rediacc/console/issues/42/comments --paginate \
    --jq '.[] | select(.user.login | test("github-actions")) | {id, created_at}'

WHAT A SUBSTANTIVE REPLY MUST CONTAIN. Go finding by finding
and for each one state exactly one of:
  - fixed: what changed and in which commit
  - deferred: where it is tracked (issue or worklist id) and why
  - disagreed: the reason, concretely, not 'out of scope'
It must be posted by someone other than @github-actions[bot] (a
second comment from the pipeline is not an answer to the
first), and it must either cite 100 or run past 200 characters.

ONE reply covers this AND check-review-comments.sh's summary
check, as long as it is posted after both comments.

To answer using gh CLI:

  # 1. Read the full report first
  gh api repos/rediacc/console/issues/comments/100 --jq .body

  # 2. Post the answer as a NEW top-level comment
  gh api repos/rediacc/console/issues/42/comments -X POST \
    -f body="Re: review report 100

  - <finding 1 title>: fixed in <sha> - <what changed>
  - <finding 2 title>: not changing - <why>
  - <nit>: deferred to <issue/worklist id>"

  # IMPORTANT: a top-level comment has NO replies endpoint. Both of
  # these return 404 (verified against the live API):
  #   repos/rediacc/console/issues/42/comments/100/replies
  #   repos/rediacc/console/pulls/42/comments/100/replies
  #     (that path is real, but only for INLINE comment ids)
  # And repos/rediacc/console/issues/comments/100 is GET/PATCH only --
  # the EDIT endpoint for the report itself. Posting there would
  # overwrite the review rather than answer it.

Or comment directly on GitHub:
  https://github.com/rediacc/console/pull/42#issuecomment-100
